{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_vrtx_01Xig34kZJ7H8JbEgWKSaamg","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. Here's what was completed:\n\n**Task:** `answers/05-005-reduce-hallucinations-in-a-medical-chatbot.md` — Q5 of 05-evaluation-metrics.\n\n**Key content written:**\n\nThe answer builds a **5-layer medical-specific hallucination stack** that distinguishes itself from the generic playbook:\n\n1. **Domain embeddings + curated retrieval** — PubMedBERT/BioLORD instead of `text-embedding-ada-002` (fixes ICD-10/drug name tokenization failures); source only from UpToDate, FDA labels, PubMed, clinical guidelines; strict cosine gate at 0.75 (vs 0.70 generic); hybrid BM25+dense for exact drug-name queries\n2. **Closed-world T=0 prompt with mandatory inline citations** — forces each claim to reference a source chunk; includes scope-restriction to \"information, not personalized advice\"\n3. **Synchronous DeBERTa NLI blocking** — not async like consumer apps; `contradiction` label → block response immediately; 50ms latency is the right tradeoff against a hallucinated contraindication\n4. **HITL tier classifier** — auto-respond for general info, log for clinical guidance, hard-block + clinician queue for patient-specific advice (personal pronouns + medication + dosage)\n5. **HIPAA-compliant audit trail** — Presidio PHI pseudonymization, S3 Object Lock for 6-year retention, 0.5% hallucination-rate SLO (vs 2% generic)\n\n**Concrete result:** 6.4% → 0.4% hallucination rate before/after domain adaptation."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":351,"cache_read_input_tokens":70496,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":351,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f4acb75f-a615-4c58-a697-d8c46380748e","uuid":"5f23676a-f2b0-4faf-9b80-0d20a4813b3a"}
